    "title": "Is Taylor Swift Going to Be in Kpop Demon Hunters 2? Ejae Says...",
    "text": "In 2025 and 2026, everyone has been all about KPop Demon Hunters and they can’t wait for the sequel to come out in a few years. They’re already prepping things, and Ejae herself, the singing voice of Rumi, said they’re down to have legendary singer Taylor Swift on board for the sequel.In a recent interview with Variety on the 2026 Oscars red carpet, ahead of the film receiving the Oscar for Best Animated Feature, Ejae revealed that there is a possibility of Swift entering the KPop Demon Hunters universe. She said, “If you want Taylor, you can come to ‘KPop Demon Hunters’ and write some songs.”More from SheKnowsRELATED: 27 Horror Movies That Have Won Oscars Over the YearsEjae at the 98th Annual Oscars held at Dolby Theatre on March 15, 2026 in Hollywood, California.While we don’t know anything else about the sequel, a Swift collab may just break the internet.In a previous interview with SheKnows, Ejae discussed her road to Kpop Demon Hunters, saying, For me, more than success, we learn more from failures. We learn more from rejection, actually. I think that’s when you grow the most. Like, working out, for example, when you’re doing a new workout routine or when you feel a muscle tear, that’s when you know, after that week of pain, it grows, and that’s you. That’s what humans are, we’re very strong.Click here to see more of our Oscars coverage, including how to watch for free, dramatic moments, and more.Before you go, click here to see all the most shocking Oscars looks over the years.Demi Moore, BjörkBest of SheKnowsSign up for SheKnows' Newsletter. For the latest news, follow us on Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram.",
